<title>USA: Vitronics Corp Q3 net falls.</title>
<headline>Vitronics Corp Q3 net falls.</headline>
<dateline>NEWMARKET, N.H. 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>For the Nine Months Ended</p>
<p>							Sep 28,     Sep 30,</p>
<p>							  1996	  1995</p>
<p> Sales					  $17,888,000 $17,070,000</p>
<p> Net income before taxes		    1,214,000   1,477,000</p>
<p> Net income after taxes			 728,000   886,000(1)</p>
<p>Net income before taxes per share:</p>
<p>   Primary					     0.11	  0.17</p>
<p>   Fully diluted				     0.11	  0.14</p>
<p>Net income after taxes per share:</p>
<p>   Primary					  0.07	  0.10(1)</p>
<p>   Fully diluted				  0.07	  0.08(1)</p>
<p> Bookings					17,594,000  18,515,000</p>
<p> Backlog					  2,561,000   4,034,000</p>
<p>Average shares outstanding</p>
<p>   Primary				     10,643,000   8,604,000</p>
<p>   Fully diluted			     10,654,000  10,588,000</p>
<p>					     For the Three Months Ended</p>
<p>							Sep 28,     Sep 30,</p>
<p>							  1996	  1995</p>
<p> Sales					   $5,814,000  $6,450,000</p>
<p> Net income before taxes			351,000     711,000</p>
<p> Net income after taxes		    141,000     427,000(1)</p>
<p>Net income before taxes per share:</p>
<p>   Primary					     0.03	  0.07</p>
<p>   Fully diluted				     0.03	  0.07</p>
<p>Net income after taxes per share:</p>
<p>   Primary					  0.02	  0.04(1)</p>
<p>   Fully diluted				  0.02	  0.04(1)</p>
<p> Bookings					 4,929,000   6,446,000</p>
<p>Average shares outstanding</p>
<p>   Primary				     10,754,000   9,548,000</p>
<p>   Fully diluted			     10,762,000  10,785,000</p>
<p>NOTE: (1) Restated to reflect earnings on a fully taxed basis.  1995 had favorable net benefit from tax loss carryforwards.  Reported net income after tax for the three month period was $675,000, and $0.07 per primary share and $0.06 per fully diluted share.  For the nine month period, net income after tax was $1,425,000, with $0.17 per primary share and $0.14 per fully diluted share.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
</text>
